    - target: {fileID: 847925133356509755, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Size
      value: 6
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 847925133356509755, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "That\u2019s Correct!\r\n\r\nThe coins in the bag are Bronze, Bronze,
        Silver, and Gold. Since we are drawing one coin, each coin has an equal chance
        of being selected.\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s list the possible outcomes:\r\n\r\nBronze\u2081,
        Bronze\u2082, Silver, Gold\r\n\r\nThere are 4 total possible outcomes.\r\n\r\nOut
        of these, 1 outcome is a gold coin.\r\n\r\nWe can calculate the probability
        using the formula:\r\n\r\nP(Gold) = \\frac{\\text{Number of gold coins}}{\\text{Total
        number of coins}}\r\n\r\nP(Gold) = \\frac{1}{4}\r\n\r\nSo, the probability
        of drawing a gold coin is 1/4 or 0.25 (25%).\r\n\r\nThe bag contains 1 gold
        coin out of 4 total coins, so the chance of drawing a gold coin is one-fourth.\r\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
