--- !u!114 &306384110
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 306384107}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a11dd23e08e5cb942a6a6b4da8d43711, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TEXDrawRuntime::TexDrawLib.TEXDraw
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_Alignment: {x: 0.5, y: 0.5}
  m_Text: "That\u2019s Correct!\n\nThe possible outcomes when rolling a fair six-sided
    die are:\n\n1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\n\nSince the die is fair, each number has an equal
    chance of being rolled.\n\nLet\u2019s define the events:\n\nEvent A: A 2 is rolled\n\nEvent
    B: A 5 is rolled\n\nLet\u2019s list the possible outcomes:\n\n1, 2, 3, 4, 5,
    6\n\nThere are 6 total possible outcomes.\n\nOut of these, 1 outcome corresponds
    to Event A (rolling a 2) and 1 outcome corresponds to Event B (rolling a 5).\n\nWe
    can calculate the probability using the formula:\n\nP(A \\text{ or } B) = P(A)
    + P(B)\n\nP(A) = \\frac{1}{6}\n\nP(B) = \\frac{1}{6}\n\nP(A \\text{ or } B) =
    \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6}\n\nP(A \\text{ or } B) = \\frac{2}{6}\n\nP(A \\text{
    or } B) = \\frac{1}{3}\n\nSo, the probability of rolling a 2 or a 5 is ( \\frac{1}{3}
    ) or about 0.33 (33%).\n\nThe die has two favorable outcomes (2 and 5) out of
    six possible outcomes, so the chance of rolling either number is one-third."
  m_Size: 6
  m_ScrollArea:
    serializedVersion: 2
    x: 0
    y: 0
    width: 0
    height: 0
  m_Padding:
    left: 10
    right: 10
    top: 10
    bottom: 10
  m_Overflow: 0
